WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.637
Modernization is usually
treated as a choice of timing.

2
00:00:03.637 --> 00:00:06.926
It isn't, because the dates
are set outside the agency.

3
00:00:06.926 --> 00:00:12.350
Federal directives already require secure
cloud configurations and better logging.

4
00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:16.637
FedRAMP's new rules become
mandatory in January 2027.

5
00:00:16.637 --> 00:00:21.271
Windows Server 2016's end of
support is January twelfth, 2027,

6
00:00:21.271 --> 00:00:25.812
and this workbook plans on those
servers being gone by then.

7
00:00:25.812 --> 00:00:29.760
But a current server still
sits in the same directory,

8
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.337
and Windows Server 2019's date
is already set for January 2029.

9
00:00:34.337 --> 00:00:36.820
So with time short, where do you begin?
